<title>CHINA: Shum Yip mulls convertible bonds issue.</title>
<headline>Shum Yip mulls convertible bonds issue.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shum Yip Investment Ltd said on Monday it is considering raising funds through a convertible bond issue but added no solid plan has been made.</p>
<p>&quot;The company is considering a possible issue of convertible bonds to raise funds,&quot; Shum Yip said in a statement. &quot;Preliminary discussions have been carried on with the company's financial advisers and no definite plan has been made.&quot;</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>Shares of the Shenzhen property developer fell HK$0.25 or 3.05 percent to end at HK$7.95 on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
